---
components: ["PeoplePicker"]
description: A people picker searches users and groups as you type and shows each choice as an avatar chip, for assigning work, sharing and inviting.
---

<script>
  import { PeoplePicker } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  const people = [
    { id: "u-1042", name: "Priya Raman", email: "priya.raman@example.com" },
    { id: "u-2290", name: "Marcus Oyelaran", email: "marcus@example.com" },
    { id: "u-3118", name: "Hannah Lindqvist", email: "hannah@example.com" },
  ];
</script>

## Basic

Pass the people to choose from as `items`, and bind `value` to read or set the people chosen. Type to search by name, email and the `secondary` line, then press <DocKbd label="Enter" /> to add the highlighted person. Each choice becomes a chip with an avatar.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerBasic" />

A person is an object with an `id` and a `name`. Everything else is optional.

| Property | Use |
| :--- | :--- |
| `id` | Identifies the person. Submitted with the form |
| `name` | Shown in the chip and the option, and used for the initials |
| `email` | Matched by the query, shown beside the name, and used to catch a duplicate |
| `avatar` | An image URL. Without one the avatar shows initials |
| `secondary` | A muted line such as a job title. Also matched by the query |
| `type` | `"group"` for a team or a list. The default is `"user"` |
| `members`, `memberCount` | The people in a group, or only how many there are |
| `disabled` | Shows the person in the menu but does not let them be chosen |

| Do | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Use for a field that names people: "assign to", "share with", "invite" | The avatar and secondary line tell apart two people with the same name |
| Use [MultiSelect](/components/MultiSelect) for a short, fixed list of roles | A picker is built for a directory too long to scroll |
| Use [TagInput](/components/TagInput) for free text such as keywords | It has no search, no avatars and no menu |
| Give the field a label | The menu takes its name from it |

## Sources

### Array

Pass an array. It is ranked as the user types: a name that starts with the query comes first, then one with a word that starts with it, then one that contains it, then one that matches the email or `secondary` line only. Accents, case and Arabic vowel marks are ignored, so `jose` finds José and `محمد` finds مُحَمَّد.

Replace the array, not its contents, to change the list: the lowercase copy that makes each key cheap is built once per array. A person already chosen is left out of the menu.

### Large lists

An array of 10,000 accounts needs no virtualization or server. A key ranks the array in one pass and stops as soon as enough names start with the query, and only the first few matches reach the DOM.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerLargeList" />

### Async

Pass a function that takes the query and returns the people, or a promise of them. The function gets `{ signal }`. Pass the signal to `fetch`, or listen for its `abort` event, to stop the request when a newer query replaces it. Only the newest request may answer: a slower, older response is dropped even when the function ignores the signal.

The function is called after `debounce` milliseconds without typing, and once with an empty query when the menu opens, so return recent people for it or set `minQueryLength`. The menu keeps the last results while the next ones load, shows a loading row after `loadingDelay`, and shows `errorText` with a retry button when the function rejects. <DocKbd label="Enter" /> retries too.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerAsync" />

### Suggestions

Pass `suggestions` to offer recent or likely people before anything is typed. They show when the query is empty, or shorter than `minQueryLength`, under the heading `suggestionsText`, without calling a function source. Press <DocKbd label="ArrowDown" /> in the empty field to open them.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerSuggestions" />

## Selection

### Multiple

The default. Chosen people are removed from the menu, so nobody is added twice. Set `max` to cap the count: a person past it is rejected with `maxText`.

### Single

Set `multiple` to `false` to choose one person. Choosing again replaces the chip, and `value` holds at most one person.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerSingle" />

### Groups

A person with `type: "group"` is a team or a list. Choosing it either adds the group as one chip, or adds its members.

| Set | Use it when |
| :--- | :--- |
| `groups="chip"`, the default | The group is the thing you save, such as an access list that should follow the team as people join and leave |
| `groups="expand"` | The people are the thing you save, such as invitees. The members come from `members`, or from `loadMembers(group, { signal })` when the group has none, and are added once each |

A group whose members cannot be read stays one chip. A group chip shows a group glyph, and its option shows `memberCount`.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerGroups" />

## Free entries

Set `allowEmail` to let the user add someone who is not in `items`. Type an address and press <DocKbd label="Enter" />, `,` or `;`. The menu offers the typed address as an option unless it names someone listed.

Paste `a@x.com, b@y.com` or one address per line to add several at once. `Ada Lovelace <ada@x.com>` and `"Lovelace, Ada" <ada@x.com>` read as a name and an address. An address that matches a known person adds that person, with their name and avatar, and a duplicate is dropped.

An entry that fails `validateEntry` becomes an invalid chip, shown in red with a warning glyph and named for a screen reader. It is not submitted, and the form cannot be sent while one is left. Set `invalidEntries="reject"` to keep the text in the field with a message instead. Entries added this way have `free: true`, and `invalid: true` when they failed.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerEmails" />

| Do | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Pass `validateEntry` to restrict addresses to your domain | The default accepts any address that looks like one |
| Let invalid chips show | The user sees which entry of a pasted list failed, and removes just that one |
| Check the address on the server too | The check here only looks at the shape |

## Display

### Collapsed chips

With more than `maxVisible` people, the field shows the first few and a "+N" chip while it has no focus, so 50 people take one line and a half and not a wall. Focusing the field shows them all, wrapped. Set `maxVisible` to `0` to always show every chip.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerCollapse" />

### Custom items

Fill the `item` slot to draw each option. It receives the `person`, its `index`, the `query` and whether it is `highlighted`. Mark the text with `bx--people-picker__name` and `bx--people-picker__secondary` to keep the ellipsis and the colors. Fill the `chip` slot to draw a chip, and spread `props` onto a [Tag](/components/Tag) so its close button keeps removing the person.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerCustom" />

## Sizes

Set `size` to match the surrounding fields. Chips and options scale with it. Inside a `Form`, the field takes the form's `size` unless it sets its own.

### Extra small

<PeoplePicker size="xs" labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={[people[0]]} />

### Small

<PeoplePicker size="sm" labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={[people[0]]} />

### Medium

<PeoplePicker labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={[people[0]]} />

### Extra large

<PeoplePicker size="xl" labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={[people[0]]} />

## States

### Invalid

<PeoplePicker labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={[people[0]]} invalid invalidText="Add at least two people" />

### Warning

<PeoplePicker labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={[people[0]]} warn warnText="Someone here is outside your team" />

### Read-only

A read-only field shows its chips without close buttons. Focusing it shows every chip.

<PeoplePicker labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={people} readonly />

### Disabled

<PeoplePicker labelText="Assignees" items={people} value={people} disabled />

## In a form

Set `name` to submit one hidden input per person: the `id`, or the address of a free entry. Set `required` to ask for at least one person. Text left in the field that never became a chip does not count, and the field says so. The field follows its form's reset.

## In a modal

The menu opens above the modal and takes the keys the field would take. <DocKbd label="Escape" /> closes the menu first and the modal on the next press.

<FileSource src="/framed/PeoplePicker/PeoplePickerModal" />

## Keyboard

Focus stays in the field while the menu is open. The chips are one tab stop, reached from the field and left again with the keys below. The field ignores a key while an IME is composing.

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| <DocKbd label="ArrowDown" /> | Open the menu, or highlight the next option, wrapping at the end |
| <DocKbd label="ArrowUp" /> | Highlight the previous option, wrapping at the start |
| <DocKbd label="Enter" /> | Choose the highlighted option, add the typed address, or retry a failed search |
| <DocKbd label="Escape" /> | Close the menu and keep the text. With the menu closed, clear the text. In a modal, it stops there |
| <DocKbd label="Backspace" /> or <DocKbd label="ArrowLeft" /> | At the start of the field, move to the last chip. The arrow flips in a right-to-left layout |
| <DocKbd label="ArrowLeft" />, <DocKbd label="ArrowRight" /> | Move between chips |
| <DocKbd label="Delete" /> or <DocKbd label="Backspace" /> | Remove the focused chip |
| <DocKbd label="End" />, <DocKbd label="Escape" /> | Return from a chip to the field |

## Accessibility

The field is a combobox: `role="combobox"` on the text input with `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls` and `aria-activedescendant` pointing at the listbox and its highlighted option. A live region announces the number of results after a pause in typing, and says when nothing matched, the source is loading or it failed. A second one announces each addition and removal and the new count. Translate both with `resultsText`, `emptyText`, `loadingText`, `errorText`, `addedText` and `removedText`.

| Do | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Keep the label, even visually hidden with `hideLabel` | It names the field, and the menu is named from it |
| Pass `secondary` or `email` for people who share a name | A screen reader hears the option's name and its detail |
| Keep `limit` at 8 or fewer unless you set `menuMaxHeight` | A menu that scrolls is a scrollable region that axe expects to be reachable by keyboard |
| Pass an `avatar` URL only for people who have one | A missing or failed image falls back to initials |
